Context
  Asked to start a tmux session with emacs -nw plus the project's DX tooling and a
  harness over the skills and other metadata, and separately to make the boundaries
  for development and the process for not holding onto changes explicit. scripts/
  wip.sh is the second half of that: the boundaries are documented, but a report is
  what makes them checkable.

Deviations
  ELPA installs into the checkout rather than relying on the user's Emacs. Geiser
  and paredit were MISSING from this machine's Emacs, so a profile that assumed
  them would have been a config that cannot work. The cost is a download on first
  run and a gitignored elpa/ tree; the benefit is that the Emacs requirement is
  self-contained and verifiable.

Considerations
  The three findings the harness surfaced are all pre-existing and none is fixed
  here -- this branch is non-deployable and touches nothing under skills/. They
  belong to roadmap A1, A7 and C5, and A1 is now better characterised than it was:
  the failure is not only that start reports success it never checked, but that it
  does not wait for the proxy at all while status is documented to run right after.

  wip.sh cannot check the thing that actually went wrong today. A commit whose
  message describes files it does not contain is not mechanically detectable, so it
  prints each commit's stat and leaves the reading to a person. That is a weaker
  guarantee than a check, and it is stated as such.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, tmux 3.6a, GNU Emacs
  30.2, as dsp-dr. Session created and torn down; geiser/paredit install verified.
